>>> notes identity --project demo --lead-runtime claude-code
The SessionStart hook (`qargi hook session-start`) appends `export QARGI_LEAD='ID'`, ID being the session id, to the file named by `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE`, so the later commands of the session know their lead identity. Tested by qargi: the line is written when `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` is set and `QARGI_LEAD` is not. Not verified: that Claude Code reads that file in a real session. Without it start the session with `QARGI_LEAD=ID` set: `feature`, `local`, `review` and `release` read it; only marshal verbs take `--as ID`. The anonymous user@host works but only warns.
exit 0
