Claude Code loads a checkout's skills from `.claude/skills` and the user's from `~/.claude/skills`; a session started with the launch line that qargi prints (`claude --add-dir DIR`) loads those of DIR too. To hide a skill without removing it, set {"skillOverrides": {"NAME": "off"}} in a settings file (user, project or project-local); qargi only reads those files.
exit 0
